w TCP SYN floods on Port 8080 remains unquantified when the service daemon is active.\\n- **Async Latency Tuning**: Investigating why Python 3.14 selector event loops add ~0.8ms overhead to the 1.0ms containment target.\\n- **Next Priority**: Benchmark C++ native memory double-buffers ([atomic_double_buffer.hpp](file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/capabilities/native_cpp_broker/atomic_double_buffer.hpp)) under 100+ thread contention.\\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n21: {\"step_index\":20,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-28T21:40:15Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Worker Reports**\\n\\nI've just received worker reports from `DeepInvestigatorWorkerL0` and `DeepInvestigatorImprovementWorker` regarding the follow-up round. Now, my focus is shifting towards verifying the message from sender `dc54417a-d5a5-4d2d-bfd1-e5524ec67801`.\\n\\n\\n**Tracking Worker Responses**\\n\\nI'm now focused on tracking the responses. The initial question was sent, triggering two L0 workers and then improvement workers. L0 worker 1 reported, then L0 worker 2 reported, and I spawned an improvement worker for pipeline 1. Now, I'm waiting for that worker and will spawn the improvement worker for pipeline 2 shortly.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"invoke_subagent\",\"args\":{\"Subagents\":\"[{\\\"Model\\\":\\\"inherit\\\",\\\"Prompt\\\":\\\"<original_task>\\\\nTask: increase redteam stress level effect to be near impossible, and fully engage all teams.\\\\n\\\\nAdditional Context:\\\\nThe user explicitly requested to escalate the red-team stress level to near-impossible edge cases, maximum Byzantine fault tolerance, extreme memory/concurrency pressure, lock-free SHM corruption vectors, side-channel attacks, AST grammar exploits, and zero-day sandbox escape vectors. Escalate testing intensity to the absolute maximum threshold.\\\\n</original_task>\\\\n\\\\n<prior_attem